{
  "id": "COMPOUND:14268 - PROTEIN:4634",
  "verbalization": "Benzocaine is implicated in the regulation of Serine/threonine-protein kinase ULK1 through a complex network of interactions. The evidence suggests that benzocaine acts as a target of 4-(3-Pyridin-2-Yl-1h-Pyrazol-4-Yl)Quinoline, which in turn targets ULK1. This pathway is consistent across multiple paths, with benzocaine linked to different targets, including the tumor susceptibility gene 101 protein and glutamine--fructose-6-phosphate aminotransferase [isomerizing], all of which are also targets of the quinoline compound. The shared involvement of 4-(3-Pyridin-2-Yl-1h-Pyrazol-4-Yl)Quinoline in targeting ULK1 indicates a potential central role for this compound in the signaling cascade. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which benzocaine influences ULK1, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
